area: router
case: 08-search-unicode-request
verification: explicit-divergence
oracle: python
projection: router
reason: the router's sentence is built by lib/router.ml, which is stdlib-only and quotes a requested name with its own single-quote pass (a provider name is backend or backend:flavour, never a quote or a backslash). A non-printable codepoint therefore reaches the projection's escape as itself, while Python's repr emits a backslash escape that json.dumps then doubles — so the two sentences differ by one backslash on a zero-width space. Same verdict, same wording otherwise: closing it means giving the router a repr, which its stdlib-only rule forbids.
